    {
      "id": "claim_985b566a8bcb4878a9cd9e3f122be76d",
      "statement": "The limit_sync store lives under $CLAUDEBAR_LIMIT_SYNC_DIR (highest priority, used by tests), else $XDG_CACHE_HOME/claudebar, else ~/.cache/claudebar; per window there is a limit-5h.d / limit-7d.d directory whose records are directories named <reset:%010d>_<pct:%07.3f>, where the fixed-width fields make lexical sort match (reset, pct) ordering and the lexically-last entry is the high-water mark.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L47-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d0b8ff60f39dc7085802fabc87c9763282fdf459c20498e7186e9388a0a1013:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L70-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:daa3d7dbde1ff630fd0c26557cb1d88645b2fe86d48e5695c7f2ba3b664fe39d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_061dc99e16464674ad62b8c1c9a714a0",
      "statement": "limit_sync record creation is an atomic mkdir (concurrent sessions write distinct names; identical values are idempotent and collapse to one), and latest_* lists the window dir, takes the lexically-highest entry, and rmdir's the rest so exactly one entry remains per window, keeping the store bounded; GC failures are ignored.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/segment/limit_sync.rs#L112-L140",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:50323a5d65a1e9ea2ed5f42e123b45558207e5a46e744b9e90b4f85b311a57ec:"
        },
        {
